  "body": "In the case where the image passed to createPattern() does not have an intrinsic size, as is the case with svg source images, there needs to be a specified default sizing behavior.\n\nThe most straightforward approach would be to use the same sizing algorithm as drawImage(), but that would mean that the pattern size would be dependent on the size of the canvas whose context was used to create the pattern.  Maybe that is is okay, or even desirable? Currently, a workaround that avoids unspecified behavior would be to bake the image at a specific resolution using an intermediate canvas.\n",
